  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A fictional group of volunteers prepares a multilingual guide for visitors attending an international youth festival.",
          "ja": "架空のボランティア団体は国際青少年祭の来場者向け多言語案内を作る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The original guide contains brief instructions, descriptions of local customs, and references to facilities near the festival site.",
          "ja": "原文には短い指示、地域の慣習、会場付近の施設への言及がある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The organizers initially ask students to translate each sentence as closely as possible to the original wording.",
          "ja": "当初主催者は各文を原文にできるだけ近く翻訳するよう学生に求める。"
        },
        {
          "en": "During a review, a student notices that an accurate translation may still leave someone uncertain about what action to take.",
          "ja": "確認中、正確な翻訳でも何をすべきか分からない場合があると一人が気づく。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A sentence tells visitors to collect a particular form at the usual reception area.",
          "ja": "ある文はいつもの受付で特定の用紙を受け取るよう伝える。"
        },
        {
          "en": "For local volunteers, the expression refers to a familiar location that requires no further explanation.",
          "ja": "地元のボランティアには追加説明不要の場所を指す表現だ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "However, someone attending for the first time may not know which building contains the reception desk or how to recognize it.",
          "ja": "しかし初参加者は受付のある建物や見分け方が分からないかもしれない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The translators recognize that the problem concerns missing contextual information rather than an incorrect choice of vocabulary.",
          "ja": "問題は語彙の選択ミスでなく文脈情報の不足だと認識する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Instead of modifying the translated version alone, the group discusses revising the original guide to make its instructions more explicit.",
          "ja": "翻訳だけを修正せず指示を明確にする原文修正を議論する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They include a simple diagram, identify the location of the reception area, and explain what visitors should do if they cannot find the form.",
          "ja": "簡単な図を含め受付の場所を特定し用紙が見つからない場合の行動を説明する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They also distinguish essential instructions from optional descriptions intended to help visitors appreciate the history of the celebration.",
          "ja": "必須指示と祭典の歴史の理解を助ける任意説明を区別する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "These changes are incorporated into every language version so that local visitors can benefit from the improvements as well.",
          "ja": "地元来場者も利益を得られるよう全言語版に変更を組み込む。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The volunteers ask imaginary readers from different backgrounds to describe what they understand from several sample sections.",
          "ja": "異なる背景の架空の読者が見本部分から何を理解するか考える。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They avoid claiming that the exercise proves that the guide will be equally accessible to every possible visitor.",
          "ja": "全来場者に同等に理解しやすいと証明する練習だとは主張しない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Nevertheless, it reveals assumptions that were previously invisible to people already familiar with the festival.",
          "ja": "それでも祭を知る人には以前見えなかった前提を示す。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The organizers decide to provide a way for visitors to request further clarification if the written explanations do not meet their needs.",
          "ja": "文書説明で必要が満たされない場合に追加確認を求める方法を設けることにする。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Translation involves transferring information between languages, but communication also depends on the knowledge shared by writers and readers.",
          "ja": "翻訳は言語間の情報伝達を伴うが意思疎通は書き手と読み手の共有知識にも依存する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "An expression may be linguistically accurate without being practically informative to its intended audience.",
          "ja": "言語的に正確でも対象読者に実用的な情報を与えない表現もある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "International cooperation can therefore encourage people to examine the assumptions embedded in their own familiar ways of communicating.",
          "ja": "国際協力は自分たちのなじみの伝達方法に埋め込まれた前提を見直すよう促し得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "In this case, translating for unfamiliar readers leads the group to improve the information available to everyone.",
          "ja": "この場合未知の読者向け翻訳が全員に利用できる情報改善につながる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
